WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.703
A mission calendar coordinates requests, approvals, crews, aircraft, payloads, locations, weather windows, maintenance, and deliverable deadlines.

00:00:08.703 --> 00:00:16.909
A scheduled slot is provisional until current conditions and readiness support a final go decision.

00:00:16.909 --> 00:00:23.126
Location and airspace review uses current official sources and site information.

00:00:23.126 --> 00:00:32.824
The plan should address permissions, restrictions, terrain, obstacles, people, property, launch and recovery, communications, and emergency landing options.

00:00:32.824 --> 00:00:38.046
Weather checks begin during scheduling and continue through launch.

00:00:38.046 --> 00:00:45.257
Wind, visibility, precipitation, temperature, lighting, and rapid change affect safety and data quality.

00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:49.982
Define thresholds and alternate dates before urgency increases.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:57.691
Crew scheduling considers qualifications, currency, fatigue, travel, duty time, site familiarity, and role coverage.

00:00:57.691 --> 00:01:06.891
A payload specialist or observer may be necessary even when one pilot could technically operate the aircraft.

00:01:06.891 --> 00:01:15.595
Aircraft readiness includes maintenance status, battery condition, firmware configuration, payload compatibility, storage, spares, and required documents.

00:01:15.595 --> 00:01:23.303
Assigning an available aircraft is not enough; it must be suitable for the mission.

00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:34.991
The final plan documents objective, route, altitude strategy, collection settings, risks, controls, communications, battery margins, emergency procedures, data handling, and abort criteria.

00:01:34.991 --> 00:01:41.207
Contingencies should simplify decisions rather than create a complicated alternate mission.

00:01:41.207 --> 00:01:44.937
Scheduling conflicts need transparent priority rules.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:55.133
Safety, emergency need, authorization, weather window, asset suitability, and business consequence should outweigh seniority or who asked most loudly.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:58.863
Record why a mission displaced another.
